        "original_id": "75fd0647-b53d-5611-9a48-fa701e3350f3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: H. L. Mencken, Albert Camus, George Jean Nathan\n- Publications: The Smart Set\n- Roles: journalist, satirist, cultural critic, scholar, philosopher, author, editor\n\nFacts:\n- H. L. Mencken was born on September 12, 1880, and he was an American journalist, satirist, cultural critic, and scholar of American English.\n- Albert Camus was born on 7 November 1913, and he was a French philosopher, author, and journalist.\n- During its heyday, The Smart Set was edited by H. L. Mencken and George Jean Nathan.\n- During the editorship of H. L. Mencken and George Jean Nathan, The Smart Set gave many up-and-coming authors their start and access to a relatively large audience.\n- H. L. Mencken died on January 29, 1956.\n- Albert Camus died on 4 January 1960.",
